  "content": {
    "id": "p12-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Suppose $n$ is a positive integer. Show that\n$$x^n-y^n=(x-y)(x^{n-1}+x^{n-2}y+\\cdots+xy^{n-2}+y^{n-1}).$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Expanding the right-hand side cancels all intermediate terms, leaving $x^n-y^n$.",
      "worked": "For $n=1$, the right-hand side is $(x-y)\\cdot1=x-y$. For $n\\ge2$, expand the right-hand side:\n$$\\begin{align*}(x-y)(x^{n-1}+x^{n-2}y+\\cdots+y^{n-1})&=x(x^{n-1}+x^{n-2}y+\\cdots+y^{n-1})-y(x^{n-1}+x^{n-2}y+\\cdots+y^{n-1})\\\\(x-y)(x^{n-1}+x^{n-2}y+\\cdots+y^{n-1})&=(x^n+x^{n-1}y+\\cdots+xy^{n-1})-(x^{n-1}y+\\cdots+xy^{n-1}+y^n)\\\\(x-y)(x^{n-1}+x^{n-2}y+\\cdots+y^{n-1})&=x^n-y^n.\\end{align*}$$\nAll intermediate terms cancel, proving the identity.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 42
  },
